, mut empty)?;\n        return borrow this.values[this.entryAt(slot)];\n    }\n\n    /// The same, to change it.\n    public fn getMut(borrow mut this, key: borrow K) -> borrow mut(this) V? {\n        let hash = this.hashOf(key);\n        var empty: usize = 0;\n        let slot = this.probe(key, hash, mut empty)?;\n        let entry = this.entryAt(slot);\n        return borrow mut this.values[entry];\n    }\n\n    /// Whether `key` is there.\n    public fn contains(borrow this, key: borrow K) -> bool {\n        var empty: usize = 0;\n        return this.probe(key, this.hashOf(key), mut empty) != null;\n    }\n\n    /// The key of entry `i` (0 ≤ i < length).\n    public fn keyAt(borrow this, i: usize) -> borrow(this) K => borrow this.keys[i];\n\n    /// The value of entry `i` (0 ≤ i < length).\n    public fn valueAt(borrow this, i: usize) -> borrow(this) V => borrow this.values[i];\n\n    /// Puts slot word `word` in the first free slot from its home; the table has room.\n    fn place(slots: borrow mut Vector<u64>, word: u64) {\n        let mask = slots.length - 1;\n        var i = truncate<usize>(word >> 32) & mask;\n        while (slots[i] != 0) {\n            i = (i + 1) & mask;\n        }\n        slots[i] = word;\n    }\n\n    /// A table twice as large (at least 8), built before it replaces the old one, so a failure changes nothing. Each\n    /// slot carries its home, so growing hashes no key again.\n    fn grow(borrow mut this) -> Result<void, AllocError> {\n        let size = if (this.slots.length == 0) 8 else this.slots.length * 2;\n        var slots = Vector<u64>.withCapacity(size)?;\n        for (k in 0..size) {\n            slots.push(0)?;\n        }\n        for (k in 0..this.slots.length) {\n            let word = this.slots[k];\n            if (word != 0) {\n                HashMap<K, V>.place(mut slots, word);\n            }\n        }\n        this.slots = slots;\n        return Ok();\n    }\n\n    /// Puts `value` at `key`: the old value if the key